The elementwise map of a two-variable approximable mapping sends a pair of elements to the neighbourhoods Z for which some neighbourhood of the first element and some neighbourhood of the second are related to Z. Codomain membership is the codomain clause of the relation, and the master neighbourhood is the master relation on the two masters. For an intersection, both witnesses are pulled back by monotonicity to the intersections of the domain neighbourhoods and then combined by the intersection clause. Enlarging the codomain neighbourhood is again monotonicity.
